    3.  Join on gene symbol + case number and retain rows where both
       measurements are present.
    4.  For every gene × sample-type pair having ≥5 matched samples,
       compute the Pearson correlation between
       log2-protein abundance and log2(FPKM+1).
    5.  “Filter out” (i.e. EXCLUDE) correlations whose absolute value
       exceeds 0.5, then report, for each sample type, the mean of the
